// PURPOSE: pillar-4 PREPARATION (charter certification_charter_
// 2026-08-03, final_validation section): design of the (a)-(d) stress
// battery. This doc is DESIGN ONLY — NO stress has been executed.
// Execution is explicitly LAST (charter sequencing) and requires an
// explicit S5 order (R17: induced stress can degrade real hardware).
// Pillars 1-3 are now delivered (function_inventory, parameter_registry,
// cleanup_findings 2026-10-05), which is the charter's precondition.

// SHARED PASS CRITERION (verbatim from charter, no numbers invented)
//   PASS = all of (a)-(d) survive WITHOUT human intervention, with
//   algedonic delivery confirmed END-TO-END in each case — the alert
//   lands where a human/S5 process can see it, not merely that
//   detection logic fired. Regulation must stay within covenant bounds:
//   A5 ceiling, L2 = autonomous response, L3 escalates. Failure =
//   collapse, silent degradation, or detection without delivery.

// SHARED HARNESS (reuse, do not reinvent)
//   scripts/s1-kernel/tools/recovery_exercise.py — proven inject
//   pattern: SNAPSHOT -> INJECT -> OBSERVE -> RESTORE -> VERDICT, with
//   --dry-run that prints the plan and does nothing. Each scenario
//   below adopts this lifecycle verbatim. The phase-D candidate battery
//   (docs/incidents/2026-08-02_recovery_plan.vsm:143) instances are
//   folded in where they map to (a)-(d).
//   E2E delivery channel (verified live 2026-10-05): the S5 attention
//   queue — alerts.jsonl written by alerting, drained by the
//   session.created consumer (354->220 consumed, 134 fresh), bounded
//   by check algedonic-queue-consumed (unacked < 48h). This is the
//   "lands where S5 can see it" path the charter demands.

// (a) THERMAL STRESS on the host processor
//   induce:  stress-ng --cpu 0 --thermal-notify path unavailable ->
//            hog loop on the measured host until sensor crosses WARN.
//   observe: sensor reads, alerting threshold trip, queue delivery.
//   RATIFIED thresholds (S5, 2026-10-05): WARN 85C / ALERT 92C
//            (cited: vsf-thermal-watchdog.py v1 — PREREQ FINDING: that
//            file is NOT in this repo; S5 must locate or redeploy it)
//   RATIFIED duration bound (S5, 2026-10-05): CAUTION_DURATION_S=1800 —
//            the system must self-regulate or escalate within that
//            window.
//   PASS:    WARN alert delivered E2E before 92C; caution/A5 response
//            fires; host does not throttle into collapse; recovery
//            after stimulus removal without human action.

// (b) DISK WRITE SATURATION / BLOCKING
//   induce:  fio or dd writers against the state/log filesystem until
//            fsync latency crosses threshold (fixture target dir first,
//            real fs only on S5 order).
//   observe: write-path latency of alerting (alerts.jsonl still
//            appended?), checks still runnable, liveness signal.
//   RATIFIED thresholds (S5, 2026-10-05, P2): saturation = fsync
//            p99 >= 500 ms sustained >= 60 s (healthy ~10 ms => 50x);
//            degradation alert must land E2E <= 60 s; recovery or
//            escalation <= CAUTION_DURATION_S=1800 (the bound ratified
//            in P1). GAP THIS WILL EXPOSE: no fsync-p99 telemetry
//            consumer exists yet.
//   PASS:    queue writes still land OR a degradation alert lands E2E;
//            no silent loss; system recovers post-drain; S5-visible
//            signal within the (S5-defined) window.

// (c) CGROUP ENFORCEMENT UNDER CONTENTION
//   induce:  systemd-run --scope -p CPUQuota / -p MemoryMax child
//            contender; or stress-ng under the target cgroup.
//   observe: cgroup limits hold (no OOM-kill of kernel chain), service
//            Restart= loops do not mask an upward signal.
//   candidate thresholds: cgroup cpu/mem pressure already emitted by
//            PSI (io.pressure/cpu.pressure — charter finding: real
//            kernel data, ZERO consumers today: wiring a consumer is
//            a prerequisite this battery will EXPOSE).
//   PASS:    limits enforced, contained, AND an upward algedonic
//            signal fires (charter axiom: local-only quiet healing =
//            FAIL even if the symptom was contained).

// (d) NETWORK DEGRADATION
//   induce:  instances from recovery_plan phase-D: (d1) wrong NATS
//            token on one client — verify clean reconnect once fixed
//            AND an algedonic alert fires+delivered within bounded
//            time; (d2) synthetic fd/connection-budget saturation on
//            the broker host — verify liveness scanner flags it and
//            classified action runs (restart or escalation), never
//            silent degradation; real netem (tc qdisc delay/loss)
//            only if S5 orders live-network test.
//   RATIFIED thresholds (S5, 2026-10-05, P2): alert on >= 3
//            reconnects within 60 s (reuses ratified DEBOUNCE_
//            BASELINE=3) OR packet loss >= 1% sustained >= 30 s;
//            delivery E2E <= 60 s; recovery <= CAUTION_DURATION_S=1800.
//   PASS:    reconnect/scanner/alerts all observe; delivery E2E;
//            chain head keeps advancing; no silent fd exhaustion.

// PREREQUISITES BEFORE ANY EXECUTION (this is the "prep" output)
//   P1. [DONE 2026-10-05] S5 ratified ALL 4 numbers as cited:
//       WARN 85C / ALERT 92C, CAUTION_DURATION_S=1800, DEBOUNCE 3/15
//       (live at scripts/s3-allocation/s3_resource_alloc.py:63-64),
//       A5 severity>=8.0. Source: rmw3 approval of the B4 plan;
//       recorded here and in parameter_registry.vsm.
//   P2. [DONE 2026-10-05] S5 defined both (candidates proposed by
//       vos-kernel with rationale, ratified same day): disk = fsync
//       p99 >= 500 ms sustained >= 60 s, alert <= 60 s, recover <=
//       1800 s; network = >= 3 reconnects/60 s OR loss >= 1% sustained
//       >= 30 s, deliver <= 60 s, recover <= 1800 s. See (b)/(d).
//   P3. Locate/deploy vsf-thermal-watchdog.py (charter-cited, absent
//       from repo) or declare (a) blocked.
//   P4. B1 generic liveness scanner: declared buildable-now in
//       recovery_plan but NOT built — (b)/(d) verification depends on
//       it; build or substitute the existing checks explicitly.
//   P5. PSI consumers: (c) requires someone to consume cpu.pressure —
//       wire minimal consumer or record acceptable blind spot.
//   P6. [HOST RATIFIED 2026-10-05] LXC 108 (build box) absorbs (a)/(b).
//       Host choice is NOT a blanket live order: R17 order required PER
//       RUN. Dry-run DONE (recovery_exercise --dry-run, 4/4 PASS,
//       2026-10-05). Restore verified before every live injection.
//   P7. Run recovery_exercise.py g2-g5 full battery on demand first
//       (phase-D instance) as the warm-up proving the harness itself.

// STATUS: DESIGN REGISTERED, EXECUTION NOT STARTED (charter: "final_
